./LOGBOOK.md:219:- FINDING, BLOCKING: the script inventory's Linux `active-process-count-limit` cell says `available: RLIMIT_NPROC`. 4.1.1's own rule "An `available` control MUST report `applied`" then *requires* every Linux manager to emit `active-process-count-limit / available / applied` in each `script-capability-evidence-v1` record. `RLIMIT_NPROC` bounds processes for the **real UID**, shared with every other process that user owns — the literal content of `no-private-aggregate-domain`, which is what the same row's macOS cell says, on a platform that has the same rlimit with the same semantics. One row, two standards for one primitive. Fix: `host-conditional: delegated cgroup v2 pids.max`, in `core.md`, `manager.md:710`, and the vectors together.
